{"schema_version":3,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"wlc:Q.123","provision":"WLC Q.123","book":"wlc","book_name":"Westminster Larger Catechism","abbreviation":"WLC","reference":"Q.123","title":"Question 123","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/wlc/q-123/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#wlc/Q.123","current_text":{"html":"<p class=\"provision-question\"><strong>Q. 123.</strong> Which is the fifth commandment?</p><p><strong>A.</strong> The fifth commandment is, Honour thy father and thy mother: that thy days may be long upon the land which the Lord thy God giveth thee.</p>","text":"Q. 123. Which is the fifth commandment?A. The fifth commandment is, Honour thy father and thy mother: that thy days may be long upon the land which the Lord thy God giveth thee."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"a37d71a35e8f9c0167937b7d42b075812156fb6a","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"613a69259d78b86fb70a893f9e1757ec3e9bad7c9b7578dfb01c4796d6a9b4fc","assessment_fingerprint":"517b100d2e9006e313ab6d84d4f0f31593b77832f395383ba2227779470cd034","assessment_summary":{"status":"stale","file":"index/provision_link_adjudications.jsonl","total":11481,"expected":12405,"applied":0,"stale":11481,"unmatched":0,"unassessed":12405},"parent_id":null,"children":[],"coverage":{"relationships":"indexed_records","recommendations":{"status":"incomplete","note":"Recommendation and study papers are not comprehensively indexed by provision."},"history":"not_available"},"relationship_count":1,"relationships":[{"id":"wlc:Q.123--case:cases/ga45_2017__2016-08.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga45_2017__2016-08.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Doty v. Nashville Presbytery","year":2017,"disposition":"dismissed","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga45_2017__2016-08.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga45_2017__2016-08.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"wlc:Q.123--case:cases/ga45_2017__2016-08.md:occ-5a4181b8a8b4","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga45_2017__2016-08.html","repository_path":"cases/ga45_2017__2016-08.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":145},"excerpt":"[^fn-ga45-p530-n21]:The charges reference Larger Catechism 123, 124, 125, 126, 127, and 128.","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga45_2017__2016-08.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["complaint standing","charges vs reports","non-member standing to complain","BCO 43-1 standing","filing charges with wrong court","reports under BCO 31-2","investigation and declination to indict"],"standard_of_review":"not_reached","case_numbers":["2016-8"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"A complainant challenged Nashville Presbytery's handling of allegations against a teaching elder. The SJC held the matter judicially out of order and dismissed it, finding the original filing with the church session was not a BCO 43-1 complaint because the session lacked jurisdiction over the teaching elder. Presbytery properly treated the allegations as BCO 31-2/34-1 reports, and the complainant, not a Nashville member, lacked standing to complain about that new action. A nine-member dissent argued the filing of charges conferred standing under prior SJC cases."}}],"history":[]}
